title: Dealing with the  <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and spd_toleration and not spd_toleration_right and chancellor_party == "Z" and not cvp_formed
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, teh <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> still holds influence.

= Dealing with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>

We are currently in a goverment held up by the toleration of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>. Which action should we take?

- @invite_goverment
- @welfare_concession
- @paramilitary_crackdown
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@invite_goverment
view-if: not constructive_vonc
title: Can we forge a "New Grand Coalition"=

Are we sure about this? President <span style="color: #808080;">Hindenburg</span> is vehemently against this move, and displeasing him may mean the end of our goverment.

- @include: Yes, hold out the olive branch!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@include
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 0; spd_toleration_right = 0; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; spd_relation += 10; left_strength += 8; pro_republic += 5; worker_spd += 4; workers_kpd -= 4; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 5; dvp_relation -= 4; dvp_right += 2; hindenburg_anger += 15

the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> has entered goverment! this improves their relations with us, and helps restore their reputation among workers. President <span style="color: #808080;">Hindenburg</span> is greatly displeased, however.

@welfare_concession
title: Increase social spending, to retain what goodwill is left in the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: This can only happen with a budget surplus.
on-arrival: welfare += 1; budget -= 1; coalition_dissent +=1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); new_middle_ddp += 1; old_middle_ddp += 1; new_middle_dvp += 1.5; old_middle_dvp += 1.5; new_middle_other += 1.5; old_middle_other += 1.5; new_middle_lvp += 3; old_middle_lvp += 3; spd_relation += 5; dvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; dvp_right += 1; ddp_right += 0.5; lvp_right += 1; hindenburg_anger += 10; economic_growth += 0.2; unemployed -= 0.2

We have increased welfare spending! Unfortunately, this harms our relations wit, and might not wish to continue these negotiations. [? if president == "Hindenburg": President Hindenburg is also losing patience with Brüning for yielding to our demands.?]

@paramilitary_crackdown
view-if: political_decree < 2 and not sa_nationwide_ban
choose-if: spd_prussia and strife >= 3 and z_relation >= 35 and not second_bruning_cabinet_seen
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not spd_prussia: We don't control the Prussian government. ?] [? if strife < 3: Paramilitary violence isn't severe enough to justify an emergency decree. ?] [? if z_relation < 35: We lack sufficient relations with Brüning. ?] [? if second_bruning_cabinet_seen: Joseph Wirth is no longer in charge of the Interior Ministry, meaning we can no longer rely on his connections. ?]
title: Crackdown on violent paramilitaries of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**far**</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**left**</span>, and restrict certain rights.
on-arrival: political_decree += 1; prussian_police_loyalty += 0.04; prussian_police_strength += 5; kpd_relation -= 6; rfb_militancy *= 0.9; rfb_strength *= 0.85; sa_militancy *= 0.96; sa_strength *= 0.96; sh_militancy *= 0.98; sh_strength *= 0.98; workers_kpd -= 1; workers_nsdap -= 1; unemployed_kpd -= 3; unemployed_nsdap -= 3; new_middle_nsdap -= 2; hindenburg_anger += 5

Carl Severing and other Prussian officials have successfully urged Brüning to issue an emergency decree expanding police authority to suppress political extremism. The decree imposes restrictions on political meetings, organizations, newspapers, and posters, all of which now require police approval beforehand.

As a result, several <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> newspapers have been banned, triggering violent clashes between their supporters and the police. [? if president == "Hindenburg": President Hindenburg has reluctantly signed the decree, but is slowly losing patience with us. ?]

@stay_course

We will not make any changes, for the sake of stability.
